<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA REVISES DOWN 97 WHEAT CROP FORECAST.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA REVISES DOWN 97 WHEAT CROP FORECAST.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's Agriculture Minister said on Thursday heavy rains and flooding had pushed down the 1997 forecast wheat crop to 6.9 million tonnes from earlier estimates of 7.1 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Last year's disastrous harvest stood at only 3.1 million tonnes.</p>
<p>&quot;If from this moment there will be no disturbing factors I think we will get 6.9 million tonnes of wheat this year,&quot; Dinu Gavrilescu told Reuters.</p>
</text>
